  "goodToKnow": "Die Krönung is a coronation: die Krönung des Königs. For centuries, German kings of the Holy Roman Empire were crowned in Aachen Cathedral, and from 1562 in Frankfurt. Figuratively, it means the crowning glory or high point: die Krönung des Abends. Ironically, Das ist ja die Krönung! means that's the last straw. Krönen means to crown, and die Krone a crown, also the currency in Scandinavia and Czechia. Plural: die Krönungen."
